            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Telugu for to unload, then the Telugu for to drop someone off."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: రిక్షా",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రిక్షా — rikṣā — \"a rickshaw\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ఆ రోజుల్లో మా తాత రిక్షా తొక్కేవాడు. ā rōjullō mā tāta rikṣā tokkēvāḍu. In those days my grandfather used to pedal a rickshaw."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A cycle rickshaw is pedalled: రిక్షా (rikṣā) తొక్కు. The motor ఆటో took its place in most towns."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "రిక్షా (rikṣā) is a loan from English rickshaw, which English shortened from a Japanese word for a man-pulled cart."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
